 "title": "DUCK",
 "category": "Sound",
 "author": "hugz202 (AE-analog-rytm-mods); MKII port: Iced-Cream",
 "license": "MIT",
 "description": "Sidechain-style pumping without the analog compressor: every audio block the other voices' analog VCA words are scaled by a gain that dips when the key track's voice hits. FX track, AMP (COMP) pressed twice: the DUCK page, SRC (OFF or the key track), DEP, ATK, HLD, REL. Global settings held in RAM (SRC OFF at power-up). The key is the source voice's own audio as the codec captured it, one block late; the delay and reverb returns are not ducked. Its knobs are the hidden HH TEST machine's parameter records, renamed. Needs core-ar2 0.4 (its page tables). Cannot share a build with comp-preview, which changes the same COMP page list. Port of AE-analog-rytm-mods 0012-duck (Analog Rytm MK1).",
 "device": "analog-rytm-mk2",
 "os": "1.74",
